{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Leadership"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "People-Oriented Roles"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le06ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "good-natured"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pleasant; friendly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are calm, good-natured and show that they can delegate tasks very effectively. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about people oriented roles. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "confrontation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a situation in which there is a lot of angry disagreement between two people or groups"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They dislike confrontation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "calm, reasonable, and not easy to upset"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Resource investigators can be described as stable, dominant and extroverted."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "likely to do something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are prone to put things down as quickly as they take them up. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "improviser"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who can do something without any preparation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Within the team, they are good improvisers in that they work well under pressure."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "personal responsibility"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the idea that people cause an \u200bevent or \u200bsituation to \u200bhappen by their own actions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They may delegate away too much personal responsibility."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to demolish"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to prove that an idea is completely wrong"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If someone produces an idea, their instinct is to build upon it, rather than demolish it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dominance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the idea of being more powerful, more important, or more noticeable than other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Team workers can be described as stable, extroverted and low in dominance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "uncompetitiveness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the \u200bability to not \u200bcompete \u200bsuccessfully"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, their uncompetitiveness and dislike of confrontation may make them seem a bit soft and indecisive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob06aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reason Clauses Using <span class=\"italic\">in that</span>, <span class=\"italic\">insofar as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">inasmuch as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">for</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to use reason clauses, you introduce them with linking words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">in that, insofar as, inasmuch as</span></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">in that</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> insofar </span>as and <span class=\"italic\">inasmuch </span>as to justify what you have just said by indicating that the statement is true. You use these words in fairly formal English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">He's quite difficult to work with, <span class=\"strong\">in that</span> he is always complaining about the job.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We are expecting a busy week <span class=\"strong\">insofar as </span>all the appointments have been booked.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The product is guaranteed <span class=\"strong\">inasmuch as </span>we will replace it within thirty days.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">for</span></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">for </span>in very formal or literary contexts only."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I was very nervous <span class=\"strong\">for </span>it was my first day.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Coordinators are traditional team leaders <span class=\"strong\">in that</span> they guide the team to what they recognize are the objectives."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They dislike personal confrontation <span class=\"strong\">insofar as</span> they tend to try and avoid it themselves and among others."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They also know most about the private lives and family affairs of the rest of the team <span class=\"strong\">inasmuch as</span> they are the most active internal communicator."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are excellent listeners <span class=\"strong\">for </span>they are able to recognize the value of each team member. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Report Verbs With That-Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use that-clauses to talk about facts or beliefs. They are common after report verbs and related nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She explained <span class=\"strong\">that the insurance policy was about to change</span>.</span>  <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Her explanation was <span class=\"strong\">that the insurance policy was about to change</span>.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "After some report verbs, you use the subjunctive (infinitive without <span class=\"italic\">to</span>) in the that-clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I suggested she <span class=\"strong\">remove </span>all references to violence in the lessons.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are calm, good-natured and show that they can delegate tasks very effectively."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's noticed that they are the most immediately likeable member of the team. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They also help and feel that others should do the same. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She explained that a good manager makes all the difference to a team."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Work with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Develop a survey that will help identify which classmates would be suited for which people-oriented roles."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make 5 questions for each of the three roles: coordinator, team-worker, resource investigator."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Interview your classmates and take notes of their responses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Next, tabulate your results with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the different characteristics of each people-oriented role."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Reveal your findings to the class based on your classmates' answers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Also, reveal which category you would belong to and explain why."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collaborate with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I develop a survey to help identify people-oriented roles for my classmates."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create questions to interview my classmates with."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I tabulate our results and reveal them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I reveal which category I belong to and explain why."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss reasons and results of an event or action related to work and jobs."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk or report about things, actions, events, or people in a work environment."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about team roles."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What skills does a people-oriented person have?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Are you a people person? Why or why not?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"